docs/architecture/2026-05-16-mcp-tool-reference.md:14:| `prepare_change` | First workflow tool for fix/add/refactor work once the area is known; returns likely edit files, symbols, tests, risks, and memory. | `query` required; optional `entry_files`, `entry_symbols`, `mode`, `budget`, `max_tokens`, `wire_format`, `render`. | Workflow bundle with ranked pivots, context, tests, risks, memory, events, handle, structured payload, and item-level retrieval relevance detail handles. | `render=json/markdown/hybrid`; `mode=auto/compact/full`; handle plus expansion target. | `budget=tiny/compact/full`, `max_tokens`, `wire_format`. | generic events; workflow events. | Stable canonical. | `daemon/crates/lattice-daemon/src/rpc/mcp.rs`, `daemon/crates/lattice-daemon/src/rpc/workflow_v2/prepare_change.rs` |
docs/architecture/2026-05-16-mcp-tool-reference.md:44:| `inspect_working_memory` | Inspects current working-memory state for a task with compact summary or diagnostic snapshot. | `task_id` required; optional `mode`, `include_excluded`. | Compact summary or diagnostic state plus checkpoint id and expansion handle. | `mode=compact/diagnostic`; expansion handle. | Mode bounds payload. | generic events. | Stable canonical. | `daemon/crates/lattice-daemon/src/rpc/working_memory_tool.rs` |
docs/architecture/2026-05-16-mcp-tool-reference.md:53:| `get_event_trace` | Returns paginated, workspace-bounded event traces for task, session, or workspace scopes. | Optional `task_id`, `session_id`, `workspace_id`, `kinds`, `since`, `until`, `cursor`, `limit`, `render_mode`. | Event page with scope, events, cursor, payloads in full/diagnostic, hashes in diagnostic. | `render_mode=compact/full/diagnostic`; event expansion handles. | `limit`, cursor pagination, filters, render mode. | generic events; returns event records. | Stable canonical Phase 8 memory tool. | `daemon/crates/lattice-daemon/src/rpc/memory_v2/get_event_trace.rs` |
docs/architecture/2026-05-16-mcp-tool-reference.md:58:| `verify_explain_memory` | Runs fresh verification checks for a durable memory or explains the last persisted report. | `memory_id` required; optional `mode`, `render_mode`. | Verification status, checks, confidence delta, expansion handle, summary lines, optional diagnostic trace. | `mode=verify/explain/verify_and_explain`; `render_mode=compact/full/diagnostic`; expansion handle. | Render mode bounds detail. | generic events; verification memory retrieval/invalidation as applicable. | Stable canonical Phase 8 memory tool. | `daemon/crates/lattice-daemon/src/rpc/memory_v2/verify_explain_memory.rs` |
docs/architecture/2026-05-16-mcp-tool-reference.md:81:Diagnostic render modes are reserved for traceability: they may include check traces, ranking reasons, payload hashes, spilled-payload row ids, or excluded candidates. Compact modes must remain bounded enough for repeated assistant use.
docs/architecture/2026-05-16-mcp-tool-reference.md:85:Workflow responses that return bundles store context handles through `context_cache` and expose `suggested_expand` targets. `expand_context` is the canonical follow-up tool and accepts a prior `handle` plus a `focus` such as a file, symbol, test, memory, or stable identity. Memory-bearing responses expose memory or event expansion handles where useful: `get_task_memory`, `verify_explain_memory`, `get_event_trace`, and `inspect_working_memory` all return handles for focused follow-up.
docs/architecture/2026-05-16-mcp-tool-reference.md:93:Other tools expose narrower controls: `limit` bounds list/search/event outputs, `hops` and `max_depth` bound graph traversal, `budget_tokens` bounds `get_task_memory`, `budget_ms` bounds synchronous consolidation, cursor pagination bounds `get_event_trace`, and render modes bound diagnostic detail.
docs/architecture/2026-05-16-metrics-report.md:10:The goal is operational, not aspirational: changes to retrieval, memory, and workflow behavior must be evaluable from a repeatable report rather than anecdote.
docs/architecture/2026-05-16-metrics-report.md:156:   - benchmark-only regressions usually indicate retrieval, test recommendation, or memory-surfacing drift
docs/architecture/2026-05-16-crate-boundary-plan.md:9:Phase 1 through Phase 7 will land as modules inside `lattice-core`, not as immediate sibling crates. The reserved crate names are still part of the contract: `lattice-identity`, `lattice-events`, `lattice-memory`, `lattice-retrieval`, `lattice-working-memory`, `lattice-consolidation`, and `lattice-verification`.
docs/architecture/2026-05-16-crate-boundary-plan.md:42:Boundary rationale: Identity sits below every later substrate, so it must not depend on events, memory, retrieval, working memory, consolidation, or verification. That keeps the dependency graph acyclic and preserves current graph and memory compatibility.
docs/architecture/2026-05-16-crate-boundary-plan.md:64:- `lattice-core::memory` only through narrow memory-id references, not memory retrieval
docs/architecture/2026-05-16-crate-boundary-plan.md:68:Boundary rationale: Events depend on identity and storage but remain below memory consolidation and retrieval. Replay readers may produce graph or memory rebuild inputs; they do not call high-level workflow code.
docs/architecture/2026-05-16-crate-boundary-plan.md:97:## `lattice-core::retrieval`
docs/architecture/2026-05-16-crate-boundary-plan.md:99:Reserved crate name: `lattice-retrieval`.
docs/architecture/2026-05-16-crate-boundary-plan.md:101:Purpose: Own Retrieval V1: task intent, anchor extraction, hybrid candidate retrieval, explainable scoring, compact/full response shaping, and diagnostic ranking reasons across graph, docs, memories, and events.
