docs/architecture/2026-05-16-crate-boundary-plan.md:130:Purpose: Own explicit per-task working memory state, included/excluded context bookkeeping, pins, evictions, expansion state, compression state, and checkpoint restore.
docs/architecture/2026-05-16-crate-boundary-plan.md:144:- `lattice-core::retrieval`
docs/architecture/2026-05-16-crate-boundary-plan.md:150:Boundary rationale: Working memory consumes retrieval results and emits events. It is task-local state, so it must not own durable memory graph semantics or identity resolution rules.
docs/architecture/2026-05-16-crate-boundary-plan.md:173:- `lattice-core::retrieval`
docs/architecture/2026-05-16-crate-boundary-plan.md:207:Boundary rationale: Verification consumes graph facts and memory evidence. It writes verification results and events, but retrieval only reads those results; retrieval must not decide trust state itself.
