docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/tasks/T29.md:1:# T29 — Phase 4 — Hybrid candidate retrieval (graph + docs + memories + events + working set)
docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/tasks/T29.md:7:**Spec anchor:** [§Phase 4: Retrieval V1](../../2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-plan.md#phase-4-retrieval-v1), [§Retrieval Engine](../../2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-plan.md#7-retrieval-engine)
docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/tasks/T29.md:12:This task delivers pipeline steps 4 through 7 from spec §Retrieval Engine: gather candidate results from every source enumerated under "Candidate sources" — exact path/symbol lookup, code graph traversal, doc backlinks/outgoing links, FTS, embeddings, event similarity, memory links, workflow similarity, recent active working memory — and produce a unified `Candidate` stream the scorer (T30) can rank. Each candidate carries its source, the resolved anchor(s) that produced it, and a preliminary `inclusion_reason` string the shaper (T31) will refine. Hot-path budgets from spec §Phase 1/§Phase 2 still apply, so per-source retrieval is bounded by configurable caps and never performs unbounded traversal.
docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/tasks/T29.md:20:> "Phase 4: Retrieval V1 — Deliverables: ... hybrid candidate retrieval from graph, docs, memories, and events ..." (spec §Phase 4: Retrieval V1)
docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/tasks/T29.md:45:7. Add `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/retrieval_v1/candidates_tests.rs` covering: each of the nine sources produces candidates for an appropriate seed; budgets are enforced (synthetic huge graph does not blow up); intent gating skips disqualified sources; bounded expansion records traversal paths; FTS, embeddings, and event similarity all participate when present; working-memory window returns the most-recent N items from the session context (interface stub acceptable here — T35 wires the real producer); empty anchor list still yields working-memory and event-similarity results when those exist.
docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/tasks/T29.md:50:- `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/retrieval_v1/candidates.rs` — `Candidate` type, per-source retrievers, orchestrator, budget enforcement.
docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/tasks/T29.md:51:- `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/retrieval_v1/candidates_tests.rs` — in-tree tests for source coverage, budgets, intent gating, bounded expansion, traversal-path recording.
docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/tasks/T29.md:55:- `test -f daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/retrieval_v1/candidates.rs` — confirms the candidates module exists at the expected path.
