docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/tasks/T60.md:1:# T60 — Phase 8 — New tools: consolidate_session + get_memory_metrics + get_event_trace
docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/tasks/T60.md:12:This task introduces the three remaining new MCP tools from spec §MCP Surface: `consolidate_session` (trigger session-level consolidation producing episode/procedure/failure-pattern proposals), `get_memory_metrics` (return the assistant-usefulness signals required by spec §Phase 9), and `get_event_trace` (return a paginated event-log slice scoped by task/session/workspace for audit and replay). Together these three tools complete the new memory surface and make the underlying substrates inspectable from any MCP client. Without them, Phase 6 consolidation runs only autonomously, Phase 9 metrics surface nothing to assistants, and the Phase 2 event log is invisible — all violations of spec §Non-Negotiable Product Properties "every background consolidation pass is recoverable, replayable, and observable" and §MCP Tool Contract Principles.
docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/tasks/T60.md:16:> "New or redesigned memory tools: …`consolidate_session`, `get_memory_metrics`, `get_event_trace`." (spec §MCP Surface)
docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/tasks/T60.md:22:> "The full event stream should not be injected into prompts. It exists for retrieval, audit, replay, metrics, and consolidation." (spec §Event Log)
docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/tasks/T60.md:41:4. Implement `get_event_trace` in `memory_v2/get_event_trace.rs`. Accept `task_id | session_id | workspace_id` plus optional `kinds: Vec<EventKind>` filter, `since: DateTime<Utc>`, `until: DateTime<Utc>`, and pagination cursor. Return ordered envelopes from the Phase 2 reader, compact-by-default (one-line summary per event) with stable expansion handles for full payload retrieval. Enforce workspace boundary checks per spec §Non-Negotiable Product Properties — never return events from a different workspace.
docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/tasks/T60.md:42:5. All three tools must support compact + full + diagnostic render modes per spec §MCP Tool Contract Principles. `get_event_trace` diagnostic mode includes payload hashes and any spilled-payload row IDs for replay.
docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/tasks/T60.md:43:6. Each tool emits the appropriate Phase 2 events: `consolidate_session` emits `MemoryConsolidated`; `get_memory_metrics` emits a `ToolCalled` + `ToolResult` pair; `get_event_trace` emits `ToolCalled` + `ToolResult` (does not emit a re-entrant event for each returned envelope — that would create a feedback loop).
docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/tasks/T60.md:45:8. In `memory_v2/admin_tools_tests.rs`, write tests that: (a) round-trip each tool's request/response through serde; (b) assert `consolidate_session` produces proposals (never direct writes), and assert proposals are addressable via `propose_memory_evolution`; (c) assert `get_memory_metrics` returns every spec-required signal name or an explicit `null` with reason; (d) assert `get_memory_metrics` never fabricates values; (e) assert `get_event_trace` enforces workspace boundary (cross-workspace request returns a typed error); (f) assert pagination cursor stability across calls; (g) assert each tool emits the correct Phase 2 events.
