docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/tasks/T19.md:12:This task replaces the legacy single-table memory model with a typed memory schema that the rest of Phase 3 builds on. It defines the full memory-class taxonomy (including `CounterMemory` as a first-class class distinct from a `contradicts` link), the SQLite DDL covering every spec-required memory field, the Rust types that mirror the schema, and an architecture doc that records the model authoritatively so later phases (retrieval, consolidation, verification) reference one source of truth. Without this redesign, memory cannot represent claims, evidence, validity conditions, or counter-claims — only loose notes — which violates the spec's core thesis.
docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/tasks/T04.md:12:This task captures benchmark numbers for the existing Lattice workflow tools so Phase 4 (retrieval), Phase 9 (metrics), and the hot-path budget assertions in Phase 1 and Phase 2 have a real baseline to regress against. Spec §Phase 0 Deliverables explicitly requires "baseline benchmark suite from current Lattice workflows." Without these numbers, later claims of "no regression" or "30 percent fewer discovery tool calls" cannot be evaluated objectively. The benchmark must follow Rust criterion conventions, run from `cargo bench`, and emit a JSON metrics file the build harness can verify.
