docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/tasks/T30.md:1:# T30 — Phase 4 — Scoring model with diagnostic mode (all required signals)
docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/tasks/T30.md:7:**Spec anchor:** [§Phase 4: Retrieval V1](../../2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-plan.md#phase-4-retrieval-v1), [§Retrieval Engine](../../2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-plan.md#7-retrieval-engine), [§Ranking Complexity](../../2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-plan.md#ranking-complexity)
docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/tasks/T30.md:12:This task delivers pipeline step 8 — the scorer — and the diagnostic mode that makes the scorer auditable per spec §Ranking Complexity. The scorer must apply every ranking signal the spec enumerates, expose each signal as a named, inspectable feature, and emit both scores and human-readable reasons under a diagnostic mode. Compact mode emits only enough explanation for an assistant to trust the result; diagnostic mode emits the full per-signal breakdown. The scorer must remain feature-based — no learned policy is acceptable in Phase 4 — so retrieval ranking stays explainable for the lifetime of this phase.
docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/tasks/T30.md:18:> "The ranker should expose scores and reasons in diagnostic mode. Compact mode should include only enough explanation for an assistant to trust the result." (spec §7. Retrieval Engine)
docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/tasks/T30.md:22:> "Risk: ranking becomes hard to reason about. Control: keep ranker feature-based and inspectable before any learned policy. Expose diagnostic scores." (spec §Ranking Complexity)
docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/tasks/T30.md:43:5. Implement `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/retrieval_v1/diagnostic.rs`: the public API for diagnostic mode. Exposes `RankingDiagnostics { intent, anchors, candidates_per_source, ranked: Vec<RankedCandidate>, weights, budget_exhaustion_flags }` plus serde derivation, so T31 (shaper) and T36 (MCP working-memory inspector) can hand the diagnostics straight to the caller without further transformation.
