docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/tasks/T35.md:12:This task implements every required operation on `WorkingMemoryState` from spec §5: `retrieve`, `summarize`, `filter`, `pin`, `evict`, `expand`, `compress`, `checkpoint`. Each operation mutates state in a documented, auditable way and pairs with a contract: every operation that drops or skips a memory must record the result in `excluded_memories` with a reason so the working-memory inspector (T36) can show what was intentionally left out. The operations integrate with Phase 4 retrieval (`retrieve` calls into the Phase 4 pipeline, `compress` invokes the shaper's compression policy, `pin` supplies the pin set the shaper honors).
docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/tasks/T35.md:20:> "Definition of done: workflow tools can show what context is active, why it is active, and what was intentionally excluded; context management is no longer just prompt accumulation." (spec §Phase 5: Working Memory)
docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/tasks/T35.md:29:  - `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/retrieval_v1/shaper.rs` and `scoring.rs` — invoked by `retrieve`, `compress`, `expand`.
docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/tasks/T35.md:31:- Standards files to honor: `/home/pete/cadres/shared/templates/coding.md` (single source of truth — no parallel ranker or shaper in this module); `/home/pete/cadres/lattice/CLAUDE.md`.
docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/tasks/T35.md:38:   - `retrieve(state, args, ctx)`: invokes the Phase 4 pipeline (intent → anchors → candidates → scoring → shaper) and merges the returned `RetrievalBundle` into `state.selected_memories`; every dropped candidate during shaper compression is captured in `state.excluded_memories` with its exclusion reason.
docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/tasks/T35.md:39:   - `summarize(state, args, ctx)`: returns a compact `WorkingMemorySummary` view (task, intent label, active file count, selected/excluded counts, budget usage, top hypotheses) for MCP display and event capture.
docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/tasks/T35.md:40:   - `filter(state, predicate, ctx)`: removes selected memories that fail `predicate`; removed entries move to `excluded_memories` with reason `"filtered: <predicate description>"`.
docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/tasks/T35.md:42:   - `evict(state, identities, ctx)`: removes identities from `selected_memories`, records each in `excluded_memories` with reason `"evicted: <caller reason>"`; refuses to evict pinned identities unless `force=true`.
docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/tasks/T35.md:44:   - `compress(state, budget, ctx)`: reuses the shaper's compression policy on `state.selected_memories`, honoring `pinned_identities`; dropped results move to `excluded_memories` with reason `"compressed: budget=<n> tokens"`.
docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/tasks/T35.md:47:5. Wire `OpContext` so it carries the SQLite connection, retrieval profile, identity resolver, and shaper handle once — operations never construct these themselves.
docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/tasks/T35.md:49:7. Add `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/working_memory/operations_tests.rs` covering: each of the eight operations is exercised; `retrieve` populates both `selected_memories` and `excluded_memories`; `pin` then `compress` proves pinned identities survive; `evict` of a pinned identity without `force` is refused; `filter` records the predicate description; `summarize` returns a non-empty view with the expected fields; `expand` increases the selected-memories count when the candidate pool widens; `checkpoint` returns an id whose `load_checkpoint` byte-matches the state.
docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/tasks/T35.md:68:- Single source of truth: retrieval calls Phase 4 (`retrieval_v1::shaper`, `scoring`); no parallel candidate or scoring code here.
docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/tasks/T35.md:69:- No broken windows: dead imports removed, every operation name expresses intent; every drop/skip path writes to `excluded_memories` with a reason.
