docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/tasks/R26.md:11:This gate certifies the cross-layer round-trip contracts between the three first-class substrates the spec names: workspace identity, event log, and memory graph. Each layer was reviewed in isolation by R10, R18, R25; this gate proves they compose. Specifically: stable identity references serialize cleanly into event payloads, those payloads round-trip back to the same identity targets, and memory records link to stable identities (not transient names) so memory survives identity refactors and event replays. This gate is the contract that the rest of the build (retrieval, working memory, consolidation, verification) can assume. A failed verdict here blocks T27 (Phase 4 start) because no later layer can be trustworthy on broken cross-layer contracts.
