ory schema redesign: all required fields from spec §Memory Graph (stable id, content, class, assertion type, scope, verification status, confidence + reason, freshness policy, validity conditions, invalidation triggers, provenance events, evidence references, linked files/symbols/docs/tests/memories, contradiction/supersession links, access history, usefulness scores, last verified state). Classes include CounterMemory.\n- T20 — first-class link records (source, target, link type, strength, reason, evidence event, created_by, created_at, verification_status). Link types: supports/contradicts/supersedes/refines/generalizes/specializes/co_occurs_with/derived_from/applies_to/validated_by/invalidated_by.\n- T21 — streams from spec §ViLoMem (code topology, workflow episodes, failure patterns, semantic repo claims, architecture decisions, user/team preferences, docs and contract state). Scope: session, branch, repo, user, organization.\n- T22 — migration from existing `memories` table. Architecture doc required.\n- T23 — CRUD + verification status transitions (unverified → in_review → verified, plus stale/contradicted/superseded/expired/invalidated).\n- T24 — tests for contradiction, supersession, replay.\n- R18 reviews Phase 2 (event log) with P99 evidence; R25 reviews Phase 3 (memory graph) with CounterMemory coverage; R26 is the contract gate for Identity ↔ Event ↔ Memory.\n\nRead the spec yourself for the exact section text and quote it. Cite spec headings precisely.\n\nWrite all 16 files, then report file count + first 3 paths confirmed via ls. Do NOT modify tasks.json, context.md, or plan.md. Do NOT implement any code.","agentId":"ac92f5b374c3f7cf9","agentType":"general-purpose","content":[{"type":"text","text":"All 16 brief files written successfully.\n\n**File count: 16**\n\n**First 3 paths confirmed via ls:**\n- `/home/pete/cadres/lattice/docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/tasks/R18.md`\n- `/home/pete/cadres/lattice/docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/tasks/R25.md`\n- `/home/pete/cadres/lattice/docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/tasks/R26.md`\n\n(Full set: T11–T17, R18, T19–T24, R25, R26.)\n\n**What was done:**\n- Read the spec (Phases 2/3, Storage Design, Memory Graph sections), the build context, the relevant tasks.json entries (lines 190–492 covering T11–R26), and the Cadres coding standard.\n- Wrote 14 task briefs and 2 review briefs at the requested paths, each following the exact template structures provided.\n- Each task file cites the matching spec heading via the anchor pattern, quotes 2–3 spec excerpts directly, lists files_expected and verification_commands verbatim from tasks.json, and gives 8–11 concrete steps tuned to the task type:\n  - T11: all 20 event kinds + envelope fields verbatim from spec §Event Log.\n  - T12: explicit column list for `events` and `event_payloads` with append-only triggers and indexes (task/session/workspace+branch/kind).\n  - T13: writer with payload hashing, spillover, workspace scoping, batched/sync flush; P99 budget called out (test sits in T17).\n  - T14: typed query builder with mandatory scope, ceilings, streaming, payload-corruption detection.\n  - T15: enumerates the workflow tools instrumented (`prepare_change`, `plan_edit`, `get_context_capsule`, `expand_context`, `get_working_set_context`, `trace_scenario`, `summarize_subsystem`, `impact_from_diff`, `diagnose_failure`, `record_workflow_outcome`, `save_observation`) and the per-event helpers.\n  - T16: daemon-managed background compactor + versioned independently-readable snapshot header + `Bootstrap::load`; architecture doc required.\n  - T17: ordering/replay/corruption/scoping/P99 tests gated with `--include-ignored` for budget tests.\n  - T19: full 13-class taxonomy including CounterMemory + every spec-required field + denormalized scope columns + architecture doc.\n  - T20: all 11 link types, four first-class tables with explicit column lists, evidence anchors with span sha256 for Phase 7.\n  - T21: seven streams + total `classify_stream` over `MemoryClass` + deny-by-default `ScopeFilter`.\n  - T22: idempotent restartable migrator with dry-run + CLI + crash recovery + architecture doc with column-mapping table.\n  - T23: CRUD + idempotency table + full verification-status state machine with allowed/disallowed transitions enumerated, every transition emits the right lifecycle event.\n  - T24: contradiction (link vs CounterMemory distinction), supersession chains + cycle rejection, replay byte-equivalence, exhaustive link-type coverage.\n  - R18: review structure with the required `## P99 budget evidence` section.\n  - R25: review structure with the required `## CounterMemory coverage` section.\n  - R26: contract gate with `## Contract surfaces`, `## Round-trip evidence`, `## Schema regression coverage`, plus the requirement to add and pass `contract_tests::identity_event_memory`.\n\nNo code was implemented; no modifications were made to tasks.json, context.md, or plan.md."}],"totalDurationMs":765124,"totalTokens":115872,"totalToolUseCount":29,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":416,"cache_read_input_tokens":114179,"output_tokens":1276,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":416},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[{"input_tokens":1,"output_tokens":1276,"cache_read_input_tokens":114179,"cache_creation_input_tokens":416,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":416,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"toolStats":{"readCount":7,"searchCount":3,"bashCount":3,"editFileCount":16,"linesAdded":1315,"linesRemoved":0,"otherToolCount":0}}}
docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/logs/T69.log:2920:docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/logs/T40.log:7323:./docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/logs/T04.log:2741:./docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/logs/00-decompose.log:806:{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_015fKcvZfgcEs97BQgrrZ5xL","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01Y7QFPHstAz9FnuCrEEM8Ld","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/home/pete/cadres/lattice/docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/tasks/T65.md","content":"# T65 — Phase 9 — Metric collection module (all required signals from spec)\n\n**Phase:** 9\n**Type:** backend\n**Model class:** balanced\n**Depends on:** R64\n**Spec anchor:** [§Phase 9: Metrics And Evaluation](../../2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-plan.md#phase-9-metrics-and-evaluation)\n**Standards:** Cadres coding standard; Lattice project rules (`/home/pete/cadres/lattice/CLAUDE.md`, `AGENTS.md`).\n\n## Goal\n\nThis task creates the canonical metrics module that collects every assistant-usefulness signal required by spec §Phase 9. Without a single module owning these signals, downstream tasks (T66 benchmark fixtures, T67 MCP surface, T68 CLI report, T69 regression tests) would each invent their own definitions and diverge. The module turns the event log + memory access history + workflow outcomes into the nine required signals named in spec §Phase 9: tool calls per successful task, irrelevant files opened per task, relevant anchor recall, memory inclusion precision, memory later-used rate, stale memory surfaced rate, contradiction missed rate, tests recommended versus tests needed, and workflow success after first plan.\n\n## Spec excerpts that drive this task\n\n> \"Required metrics: tool calls per successful task; irrelevant files opened per task; relevant anchor recall; memory inclusion precision; memory later-used rate; stale memory surfaced rate; contradiction missed rate; tests recommended versus tests needed; workflow success after first plan.\" (spec §Phase 9)\n\n> \"Phase 9 Deliverables: retrieval relevance metrics; memory usefulness metrics; context token efficiency metrics; stale/contradicted memory surfacing metrics; test-pass-after-plan metrics; repeated-failure reduction metrics; benchmark tasks with golden expected anchors; regression dashboard or CLI report.\"\n\n> \"Definition of done: changes to retrieval, memory, and workflow behavior can be evaluated without relying on anecdote.\" (spec §Phase 9)\n\n## Inputs\n\n- Dependency outputs: R64 (MCP contract gate) — metric collection depends on a stable tool surface so signal definitions reference canonical tool names from T61.\n- Existing repo files this task builds on:\n  - `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/events/` — Phase 2 event reader; all metrics derive from event aggregation.\n  - `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/memory/` — Phase 3 memory accesses, scores, evidence; used for memory-related signals.\n  - `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/verification/` — Phase 7 verification statuses; used for stale-surfaced and contradiction-missed signals.\n  - `daemon/crates/lattice-daemon/src/rpc/session_metrics.rs` — current per-session telemetry; T65 supersedes its partial coverage with a complete spec-aligned set.\n  - `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/intelligence/record_workflow_outcome.rs` and the T62 outcome recorder — source for workflow success signals.\n  - Phase 1 identity types (every signal references stable IDs, never names).\n- Standards: Cadres coding standard `## Hard limits`, `## Single source of truth`, `## No broken windows`, `## Schema / model parity`, `## Observability`, `## Tests as documentation`.\n\n## Steps\n\n1. Read spec §Phase 9 in full. Quote the \"Required metrics\" paragraph verbatim into a doc comment on `metrics/signals.rs` so the canonical list is preserved at the call site.\n2. Create `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/metrics/mod.rs` exporting `signals`, the `MetricSignal` enum, the `MetricValue` struct, and the `MetricsCollector` aggregator. Doc-comment the module with a reference to spec §Phase 9.\n3. In `metrics/signals.rs`, define `pub enum MetricSignal` with one variant per spec-required signal: `ToolCallsPerSuccessfulTask`, `IrrelevantFilesOpenedPerTask`, `RelevantAnchorRecall`, `MemoryInclusionPrecision`, `MemoryLaterUsedRate`, `StaleMemorySurfacedRate`, `ContradictionMissedRate`, `TestsRecommendedVsNeeded`, `WorkflowSuccessAfterFirstPlan`. Derive `Serialize`, `Deserialize`, `Clone`, `Copy`, `Debug`, `PartialEq`, `Eq`, `Hash`. Implement `MetricSignal::as_str()` returning the canonical snake_case wire name used by the T67 MCP surface and the T68 CLI report.\n4. Define `pub struct MetricValue { signal: MetricSignal, value: Option<f64>, denominator: Option<u64>, sample_count: u64, source: MetricSource, computed_at: DateTime<Utc>, reason_if_null: Option<String> }`. The `Option<f64>` value supports honest reporting when no data is available — never fabricate zeros. The `source` field discriminates `EventLog`, `MemoryStore`, `WorkflowOutcome`, `Verifier`, `SessionMetrics`.\n5. In `metrics/signals.rs`, implement a deterministic collector function per signal that aggregates from the appropriate source(s):\n   - `ToolCallsPerSuccessfulTask` — count `ToolCalled` events per `task_id` whose terminal event is `WorkflowSucceeded`; mean across tasks in scope.\n   - `IrrelevantFilesOpenedPerTask` — count `FileRead` events per task where the file was not part of the eventual `PatchApplied` or `WorkflowSucceeded` artifact set.\n   - `RelevantAnchorRecall` — fraction of golden anchors (from T66 fixtures) that appear in the workflow's `ContextBundleReturned` anchor list.\n   - `MemoryInclusionPrecision` — fraction of `MemoryRetrieved` entries that were subsequently referenced (`MemoryExpanded`, cited by `PatchApplied`, or referenced by a later `WorkflowSucceeded`).\n   - `MemoryLaterUsedRate` — fraction of retrieved memories that the consumer used downstream within the same session or a subsequent reuse window.\n   - `StaleMemorySurfacedRate` — fraction of `MemoryRetrieved` entries whose verification status was `stale` and that lacked a stale label in the response payload.\n   - `ContradictionMissedRate` — fraction of memory inclusions where a contradiction link existed but was not surfaced.\n   - `TestsRecommendedVsNeeded` — comparison between `find_relevant_tests` output and the test set actually required to detect the patch (golden answer from T66).\n   - `WorkflowSuccessAfterFirstPlan` — fraction of tasks where the first `PlanCreated` event led to `WorkflowSucceeded` without a `WorkflowFailed` in between.\n6. Implement `pub struct MetricsCollector { … }` exposing `collect(scope: MetricScope, signals: &[MetricSignal]) -> Vec<MetricValue>`. `MetricScope` mirrors the §Memory Graph scope taxonomy (`session | branch | repo | user | organization`) plus an optional time range.\n7. Honor the spec §Non-Negotiable Product Properties bounds: no unbounded event-log scan on hot paths. Every collector applies a scope filter and a configurable maximum sample size, with explicit `incomplete: true` on the `MetricValue` when truncated.\n8. In `metrics/signals_tests.rs`, write tests that: (a) every `MetricSignal` variant has a deterministic collector; (b) collectors return `None` with a reason when no data is available rather than fabricating zero; (c) each collector returns the spec-defined value on a hand-crafted event fixture; (d) scope filters prevent cross-scope leakage; (e) sample-size bounds are honored.\n\n## Files expected\n\n- `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/metrics/mod.rs` — module root exporting `signals`, `MetricSignal`, `MetricValue`, `MetricSource`, `MetricsCollector`, `MetricScope`; doc-comment cites spec §Phase 9.\n- `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/metrics/signals.rs` — `MetricSignal` enum with all nine spec-required variants, `MetricValue` struct, deterministic collector implementations, scope and sample-size bounds.\n- `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/metrics/signals_tests.rs` — unit tests covering deterministic collectors, honest null reporting, fixture-derived correct values, scope-filter enforcement, sample-size bounds.\n\n## Verification\n\n- `test -f daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/metrics/mod.rs` — confirms the module root file exists at the harness path.\n- `test -f daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/metrics/signals.rs` — confirms the signals file exists at the harness path.\n- `cd daemon && cargo test -p lattice-core --lib metrics::signals_tests` — every metric-signal test passes (deterministic collectors, honest null, fixture correctness, scope filters, sample-size bounds).\n\n## Coding-standard checks\n\n- File length ≤800 lines per file (split `signals.rs` per signal family if it grows beyond, e.g. `signals/tool_usage.rs`, `signals/memory.rs`).\n- Function length ≤50 lines, nesting ≤3, cyclomatic ≤10.\n- Schema parity: `MetricSignal`, `MetricValue`, `MetricSource`, `MetricScope` derive `Serialize`, `Deserialize`, `Debug`, `Clone`; every public field has a doc comment; wire names match the strings used by T67/T68.\n- No silent error handling — missing data produces `None` with a `reason_if_null` string, never a fabricated zero.\n- No `TODO`, `FIXME`, `XXX`, commented-out code; no unjustified `#[allow(...)]`.\n- Public API names follow intent-over-mechanism naming (`MetricSignal::RelevantAnchorRecall`, not `MetricSignal::AnchorRec`).\n- For SQLite: queries go through Phase 2/3/7 APIs; no raw SQL in the metrics module.\n- Observability: collectors emit `tracing::debug!` spans with `signal`, `scope`, `sample_count`, `incomplete` fields.\n- Doc citation: cite spec headings `## Phase 9: Metrics And Evaluation`, `## Event Log`, `## Memory Graph`, `## Verification Engine` in module doc comments.\n\n## Definition of done\n\n- [ ] Every file in \"Files expected\" exists with real content (no stubs).\n- [ ] Every verification command in tasks.json passes from repo root.\n- [ ] Coding-standard checks satisfied.\n- [ ] No deferred work: every one of the nine spec §Phase 9 \"Required metrics\" signals is collected by this task — no signal is punted to T67 or T68.\n- [ ] If a backward-incompatible change was needed, the AGENTS.md \"Backward-compatibility and contract discipline\" section was followed; the existing `session_metrics` module retains its current API as a deprecation shim until T67 wires the canonical surface through MCP.\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3516,"cache_read_input_tokens":92137,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":3516,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":51,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_012n7S8LWZzY1cvitTHPzudV","session_id":"88204e0b-a61b-4ed7-ba98-4fcc53be0768","uuid":"3cf115cb-be58-4e98-bfce-c64ff2fe93eb","request_id":"req_011Cb7NM9YiaUaTnV73t6JP7","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Write Phase 8+9+Gate task briefs"}
