docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/tasks/T71.md:12:This task lays the foundation for the entire Phase 10 review surface. It registers a new VS Code webview view under the existing `viewsContainers.activitybar.lattice` slot in `extension/package.json`, wires a typed JSON-RPC bridge that translates the new memory/event/verification tool responses into UI state, and bootstraps the i18n catalog that every later subview (T72–T76) depends on. Without this scaffolding, the memory inbox, promotion queue, contradiction queue, stale view, event trace view, retrieval explanation view, consolidation queue, indexing health, and graph health subviews have no parent panel, no transport, and no string catalog. Spec §10 names the surface explicitly: "This can be a VS Code extension panel or local web UI. It should be a review and trust surface, not the center of the product." This task delivers that panel skeleton.
