docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/tasks/T71.md:38:5. Create `extension/src/review/rpcBridge.ts` exporting a typed `ReviewRpcBridge` class wrapping the existing `daemon.ts` client. Expose typed methods for the new tools introduced in Phases 6–9 (memory inbox listing, promotion queue, contradiction queue, stale memory, evidence inspection, event trace, retrieval explanation, consolidation queue, indexing health, graph health). Every method returns a `Promise<Result>` shape with explicit error variants — never swallow errors (`coding.md` §Error handling).
docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/tasks/T75.md:1:# T75 — Phase 10 — Event trace view + retrieval explanation view
docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/tasks/T75.md:12:This task delivers two diagnostic surfaces: the event trace view (operator-facing renderer for the append-only event log filtered by session/task/workspace) and the retrieval explanation view (renders the ranking scores + reasons emitted by the Phase 4 retrieval diagnostic mode). They are the surfaces operators use to answer two binding questions: "what actually happened in this session?" (event trace) and "why did this context get included and that other thing get excluded?" (retrieval explanation). Spec §10 lists both as required; spec §7 requires the ranker to expose scores and reasons in diagnostic mode, which is the data shape this UI consumes.
