docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/logs/T75.log:6253:docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/tasks/T15.md:12:This task instruments the JSON-RPC / MCP handler and every existing workflow tool so each invocation emits the right event sequence: `AssistantTaskStarted` (when a session/task begins), `ToolCalled` (on dispatch), `ToolResult` (on return), plus the workflow-specific outcome events (`ContextBundleReturned`, `MemoryRetrieved`, `MemoryExpanded`, `PlanCreated`, `WorkflowSucceeded`, `WorkflowFailed`, etc.). All events use the stable identities from Phase 1 — never transient names. Capture must be non-blocking on the hot path, must not hide tool errors, and must respect the workspace scope of the calling session. This task is the bridge that lets every later capability (consolidation, retrieval explanations, metrics) reference real history.
docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/logs/T75.log:6290:docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/tasks/T02.md:16:> "The correct abstraction is not memory attached to a code graph. The correct abstraction is a workspace cognition substrate with three first-class sources of truth: 1. Workspace graph: files, symbols, docs, tests, dependencies, routes, schemas, build targets, runtime surfaces, and ownership boundaries. 2. Event log: every assistant action, tool call, context bundle, edit, diagnostic, test result, user correction, deployment step, and outcome. 3. Memory graph: durable typed claims over the workspace and event history, with evidence, freshness, contradiction, supersession, use history, and retrieval explanations."
docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/logs/T75.log:6321:docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/tasks/T77.md:12:This task delivers the VS Code integration smoke tests that prove the Phase 10 review surface activates cleanly inside a real VS Code instance, the review panel registers, and each of the six subviews (memory inbox, promotion queue, contradiction queue, stale view, evidence inspector, event trace, retrieval explanation, consolidation queue, indexing health, workspace graph health) mounts and renders without throwing. Spec §Testing Requirements lists "extension compile/UI smoke tests" as a required test family; this task makes that test family green for the Phase 10 deliverables. Without it, regressions in webview wiring would land unnoticed because compile + lint cannot catch runtime mount failures.
