docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/results/T62.md:32:- Replacing the old generic workflow outcome path initially dropped `PlanCreated` emission for planning tools; this was restored inside the new recorder so the event sequence remained compatible.
docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/results/T24.md:36:- The existing memory lifecycle events did not carry enough state to rebuild `memories`, `memory_links`, and `memory_evidence` from the event log. I added replay snapshot payload support to `MemoryCreated`, `MemoryUpdated`, and `MemoryInvalidated`, plus reserved-event-id support in the event writer so snapshots can include the final persisted event references exactly.
docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/results/R25.md:184:- `MemoryStore::write_transition` reuses `MemoryUpdated`/`MemoryInvalidated` for `Stale`/`Contradicted`/`Superseded` transitions. Functionally correct, but Phase 4 retrieval may want a typed transition discriminator. Recorded as F-7.
