docs/architecture/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-architecture.md:60:The graph continues to answer exact identity lookup, bounded neighborhood traversal, impact analysis, backlinks, and freshness queries. What changes is breadth and identity discipline, not the fundamental responsibility boundary.
docs/architecture/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-architecture.md:122:The Phase 2 reader is intentionally scope-bound. Every query must anchor on `task_id`, `session_id`, or the `workspace_id + branch` pair; unscoped reads are rejected before SQLite runs. Queries default to 1000 rows and reject requests above 10,000 rows so retrieval, verification, and metrics workflows cannot accidentally turn the event log into a full-scan substrate.
docs/architecture/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-architecture.md:174:Each link carries source, target, strength, reason, evidence event, creator, creation time, and verification status.
docs/architecture/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-architecture.md:182:- verification status describes current trust state
docs/architecture/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-architecture.md:183:- freshness policy and validity conditions explain when the claim should be rechecked
docs/architecture/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-architecture.md:184:- contradiction and supersession state remain explicit instead of hidden in ranking
docs/architecture/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-architecture.md:194:- a `CounterMemory` record is its own claim with evidence, scope, verification, and lifecycle
docs/architecture/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-architecture.md:197:Use a contradiction edge when the relationship is enough. Use `CounterMemory` when the counter-claim must be retrieved, reviewed, and verified as a standalone fact.
docs/architecture/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-architecture.md:208:Phase 7 freshness metadata also stays on the memory row as additive compatibility fields rather than a parallel verification-state table. `expires_at` gives time-bound memories an explicit expiry threshold, while `last_verified_graph_snapshot_id` records which post-index graph snapshot last re-validated the memory. The incremental verifier uses those fields together with `memory_evidence` reference narrowing so graph deltas verify only impacted memories, and successful verification still lands through proposal application instead of direct writes.
docs/architecture/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-architecture.md:224:Ranking is shared third. Retrieval across graph, events, and memories must use one explainable scoring model family with task compatibility, identity anchors, proximity, verification, freshness, contradiction state, usefulness, and token cost as first-class signals. Memory ranking cannot ignore graph proximity, and graph ranking cannot ignore validated memory or event evidence. This is the core operational consequence of [## Design Thesis](../plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-plan.md#design-thesis).
