docs/architecture/2026-05-16-memory-graph-schema.md:120:Scope queries are deny-by-default:
docs/architecture/2026-05-16-memory-graph-schema.md:122:- A query without an explicit `ScopeFilter` is underspecified and must not
docs/architecture/2026-05-16-memory-graph-schema.md:123:  return cross-scope data.
docs/architecture/2026-05-16-memory-graph-schema.md:124:- `ScopeFilter::to_sql_predicate()` targets the denormalized scope columns
docs/architecture/2026-05-16-memory-graph-schema.md:125:  (`scope_session_id`, `scope_branch`, `scope_workspace_id`, `scope_user_id`,
docs/architecture/2026-05-16-memory-graph-schema.md:126:  `scope_org_id`) and binds every identifier as a parameter. Formatting
docs/architecture/2026-05-16-memory-graph-schema.md:127:  user-supplied scope ids into SQL is forbidden.
docs/architecture/2026-05-16-memory-graph-schema.md:128:- A `ScopeFilter` can include multiple explicit scopes, for example branch plus
