docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/tasks/R55.md:12:This task is the cross-layer contract gate between the Memory Graph (R25, Phase 3), the Retrieval Engine (R33, Phase 4), and the Verification Engine (R54, Phase 7). It proves that the three subsystems agree on three contract surfaces — `VerificationStatus` round-trips losslessly between memory and verification; `ScopeFilter` reaches every retrieval path; and `BundleProducer` / `SurfacedBundle` (T52) is the single way retrieval surfaces memory results — and that none of the three Phase 8 workflow tools can ship until the contracts hold. The review ships a new contract test file under `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/contract_tests/` that exercises all three round-trips end-to-end against the real subsystems.
docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/tasks/R55.md:20:> §Risks — Scope Leakage: "scope-aware queries, enforced filters in store APIs, and negative tests."
docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/tasks/R55.md:22:> §Retrieval Engine: "Ranking signals: ... verification status; freshness; scope; ... contradiction/supersession state ..."
docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/tasks/R55.md:28:  - `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/memory/` — `VerificationStatus` column, `ScopeFilter` plumbing.
docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/tasks/R55.md:30:  - `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/query/` — retrieval pipeline; must consume `ScopeFilter` and produce results via `BundleProducer`.
docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/tasks/R55.md:39:   - **ScopeFilter round-trip:** every retrieval entry point requires a `ScopeFilter` and applies it through `MemoryStore::list_memories(filter, …)` — no public retrieval API may accept a request without a filter.
docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/tasks/R55.md:42:4. Author `contract_tests/memory_verification_retrieval.rs` with a fixture harness seeding the full Phase 3 + Phase 4 + Phase 7 stack against a temp SQLite store. The fixture seeds memories spanning every `VerificationStatus`, every scope, and a mix of evidence kinds (file / symbol / doc / test) so contract checks have material to assert on.
docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/tasks/R55.md:44:6. Write `test_scope_filter_round_trip_for_all_scope_kinds`: for each scope (session / branch / repo / organization), construct a non-matching `ScopeFilter`, call the retrieval API, assert zero leaked rows and a `MemoryScopeFiltered` event per attempt.
