docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/tasks/T21.md:1:# T21 — Phase 3 — Memory stream taxonomy + scope enforcement helpers (deny-by-default)
docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/tasks/T21.md:12:This task carves the memory graph into the typed streams the spec calls out (code topology, workflow episodes, failure patterns, semantic repo claims, architecture decisions, user/team preferences, docs and contract state) and provides the scope-enforcement helpers that make sure every query is deny-by-default: a query without an explicit scope returns nothing, and cross-scope leakage (branch-only memory appearing in another branch, user memory leaking across users) is impossible at the store API. Without this task, retrieval (Phase 4) cannot ask "give me only architecture-decision memories for this branch" and verification (Phase 7) cannot enforce the spec's scope-leakage control.
docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/tasks/T21.md:16:> "ViLoMem's transferable idea is dual-stream memory and retrieval. For code agents, generalize that to multiple typed memory streams: code topology, workflow episodes, failure patterns, semantic repo claims, architecture decisions, user/team preferences, docs and contract state. Each stream should have its own ranking rules, freshness semantics, and consolidation policy."
docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/tasks/T21.md:18:> "scope: session, branch, repo, user, organization"
docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/tasks/T21.md:20:> "Risk: user/org/branch memories leak into wrong workspaces. Control: scope-aware queries, enforced filters in store APIs, and negative tests."
docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/tasks/T21.md:24:- Dependency outputs: T19 — `MemoryClass`, `MemoryScope`, `MemoryRecord`, schema with denormalized `scope_*` columns.
docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/tasks/T21.md:26:  - `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/memory_graph/classes.rs` (T19) — `MemoryClass`, `MemoryScope`.
docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/tasks/T21.md:27:  - `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/memory_graph/schema.sql` (T19) — denormalized scope columns that scope helpers query against.
docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/tasks/T21.md:28:  - Existing scope conventions in `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/storage/` for workspace and branch identifiers.
docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/tasks/T21.md:44:3. Define per-stream policy records: `pub struct StreamPolicy { stream: MemoryStream, freshness_default: FreshnessPolicy, consolidation_window: Duration, default_scope: MemoryScope, ranking_profile: RankingProfileRef }`. `RankingProfileRef` is a string id that retrieval (Phase 4) will resolve; do not embed ranking logic here.
docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/tasks/T21.md:46:5. In `memory_graph/scope.rs`, define `pub struct ScopeFilter` as a typed builder: `session(session_id)`, `branch(workspace_id, branch_ref)`, `repo(workspace_id)`, `user(user_id)`, `organization(org_id)`. Builder methods consume `self` and return `Self`.
docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/tasks/T21.md:47:6. Define `pub fn ScopeFilter::to_sql_predicate(&self) -> ScopePredicate` returning a parameterized WHERE clause and bind vector keyed against the denormalized `scope_*` columns from T19. Never `format!` user-supplied scope ids into SQL.
docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/tasks/T21.md:48:7. Define `pub fn ScopeFilter::enforce_subset(of: &ScopeFilter) -> Result<(), ScopeError>` so a Phase 4 retrieval request cannot widen scope beyond what the session is allowed to see (e.g. a branch-scoped request cannot read org-scoped memory unless explicitly opted in by policy).
docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/tasks/T21.md:49:8. Implement deny-by-default in the store APIs by requiring `ScopeFilter` on every read path: `MemoryStore::query(..., scope: &ScopeFilter)` — calling without a scope is a compile error. For internal admin/migration paths add `MemoryStore::query_unscoped_admin(...)` with a function name that makes the contract explicit and document it as test-or-migration-only.
docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/tasks/T21.md:50:9. Define `pub enum ScopeError { Underspecified, CrossScopeViolation { requested: MemoryScope, allowed: MemoryScope }, IdentityMismatch { field: &'static str } }`.
docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/tasks/T21.md:51:10. In `memory_graph/scope_tests.rs`, write tests covering: a query without a scope fails to compile or returns `Underspecified` (depending on whether the API takes `&ScopeFilter` directly); branch A's memory never appears in branch B's results; user A's memory never appears in user B's results; org-scoped memory only appears when explicitly enabled by `ScopeFilter::with_organization`; `enforce_subset` rejects widening; `classify_stream` mapping is exhaustive over `MemoryClass` (use a `match` with no `_` arm so the compiler enforces this).
docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/tasks/T21.md:56:- `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/memory_graph/scope.rs` — `ScopeFilter` builder, `to_sql_predicate`, `enforce_subset`, `ScopeError`.
docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/tasks/T21.md:57:- `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/memory_graph/scope_tests.rs` — stream classification exhaustiveness, scope leakage negative tests, subset enforcement, admin-path tests.
docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/tasks/T21.md:62:- `test -f daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/memory_graph/scope.rs` — scope module exists.
docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/tasks/T21.md:63:- `cd daemon && cargo test -p lattice-core --lib memory_graph::scope_tests` — scope and stream tests pass.
