docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/tasks/T31.md:12:This task delivers pipeline steps 9 and 10: deduplicate and compress the ranked candidate set, then return a compact bundle in which **every result carries an `inclusion_reason` and an `expansion_handle`**. Per spec §Phase 4 scope constraint, the shaper's output schema must be forward-compatible with the Phase 5 working-memory checkpoints — Phase 5 layers state semantics on top of these bundles without rewriting the Phase 4 schema. The inclusion-reason discipline is the non-negotiable property the R33 review will check: no bundle ships a result without one, and no result ships an expansion handle that points to a non-existent identity.
docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/tasks/T31.md:20:> "Scope constraint: Phase 4 retrieval must not depend on the formal working memory state model defined in Phase 5. Retrieval returns bundles into the calling context; working memory formalization is layered on top in Phase 5. Design the retrieval output schema to be forward-compatible with working memory checkpoints without requiring a Phase 4 rewrite." (spec §Phase 4: Retrieval V1)
docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/tasks/T31.md:36:1. Re-read spec §Retrieval Engine pipeline steps 9–10, §Non-Negotiable Product Properties bullets on inclusion reasons and expansion handles, and §Phase 4 scope constraint on forward compatibility with Phase 5 working memory.
docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/tasks/T72.md:12:This task delivers the memory inbox — the operator's primary list view over every memory the daemon knows about. It mounts inside the review panel scaffolding from T71, lists memories with filterable columns (status, scope, class), and renders one status badge per row covering all eight verification states from spec §Verification Engine. The inbox is the entry point operators use to find the memory they want to verify, accept, reject, or inspect — without it, the promotion queue (T73), contradiction queue (T73), stale view (T74), and evidence inspector (T74) have nothing to link to. Spec §10 lists "memory inbox" first among the required operator views, which fixes its position as the spine of the review surface.
docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/tasks/T72.md:16:> "Required operator views: memory inbox; proposed promotions; proposed contradictions; stale memory list; memory evidence view; event trace view; retrieval explanation view; usefulness metrics; workspace graph health; indexing health; consolidation queue." (spec §10)
docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/tasks/T72.md:20:> "Each memory record requires: stable id; content; memory class; assertion type; scope: session, branch, repo, user, organization; verification status; confidence and confidence reason; freshness policy; ... last verified state." (spec §4 — drives the filter axes)
docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/tasks/T72.md:27:  - `extension/src/review/rpcBridge.ts` — typed `listMemories({ status?, scope?, class? })` method this view calls.
docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/tasks/T72.md:35:3. Build the inbox UI inside the webview as a sortable table with columns: `Status` (badge), `Class`, `Scope`, `Content (truncated)`, `Last Verified`, `Confidence`, `Actions` (View Evidence, Open Trace). Render the table via the table primitives exposed by T71's scaffolding; use the `SortableHeader` + `useTableSort` equivalents for the webview context.
docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/tasks/T72.md:36:4. Above the table render a filter bar with three controls: `Status` (multi-select over the eight statuses from §8), `Scope` (multi-select over `session`, `branch`, `repo`, `user`, `organization` from §4), `Class` (multi-select over the memory classes from §4 including `Observation`, `Decision`, `Constraint`, `Pattern`, `AntiPattern`, `WorkflowOutcome`, `FailurePattern`, `Procedure`, `Preference`, `ArchitectureInvariant`, `DocsContract`, `OpenQuestion`, `CounterMemory`). Each control is a `vscode.window.showQuickPick` invocation triggered from a button (no raw `<select>`); the chosen values post back to the webview which re-queries the bridge.
docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/tasks/T72.md:48:- `extension/src/review/components/StatusBadge.ts` — single-source-of-truth status badge with all eight verification statuses from spec §8 mapped to color tokens and i18n labels.
