docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/logs/T15.log:1650:Read the task file. Execute every item in scope. Do not work outside the declared task scope unless a small integration fix is required for the task verification to pass.
docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/logs/T15.log:1686:This task instruments the JSON-RPC / MCP handler and every existing workflow tool so each invocation emits the right event sequence: `AssistantTaskStarted` (when a session/task begins), `ToolCalled` (on dispatch), `ToolResult` (on return), plus the workflow-specific outcome events (`ContextBundleReturned`, `MemoryRetrieved`, `MemoryExpanded`, `PlanCreated`, `WorkflowSucceeded`, `WorkflowFailed`, etc.). All events use the stable identities from Phase 1 — never transient names. Capture must be non-blocking on the hot path, must not hide tool errors, and must respect the workspace scope of the calling session. This task is the bridge that lets every later capability (consolidation, retrieval explanations, metrics) reference real history.
