docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/logs/T59.log:1650:Read the task file. Execute every item in scope. Do not work outside the declared task scope unless a small integration fix is required for the task verification to pass.
docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/logs/T59.log:1686:This task introduces the unified `verify_explain_memory` MCP tool (collapsing the spec's `verify_memory` + `explain_memory` per §MCP Surface "Tool surface discipline") and the new `list_memory_conflicts` tool. The unified tool runs verification checks against a memory and returns both the resulting status (`verified` | `unverified` | `in_review` | `stale` | `contradicted` | `superseded` | `expired` | `invalidated`) and a structured explanation of why each linked file/symbol/doc/test contributed to that status. `list_memory_conflicts` surfaces all contradiction and supersession edges anchored on a target memory or graph node so an operator can review them. Both tools are required by spec §MCP Surface and are the trust surface for the verification engine — without them, the Phase 7 verifier produces statuses that no assistant or operator can interrogate.
docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/logs/T59.log:1696:> "Every memory-bearing response should identify: why the memory was included; evidence strength; verification status; freshness status; contradiction/supersession state; scope; expansion target." (spec §MCP Tool Contract Principles)
docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/logs/T59.log:1702:  - `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/verification/` — Phase 7 verifier (existence, span, scope, expiry checks; incremental verification jobs).
docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/logs/T59.log:1713:2. Implement `verify_explain_memory` in `memory_v2/verify_explain_memory.rs` as the unified tool. Accept `memory_id: MemoryId` plus optional `mode: "verify" | "explain" | "verify_and_explain"` (default `verify_and_explain`). Internally run the Phase 7 verifier on the memory, then construct an `ExplainReport` that itemizes each verification check (linked file exists, linked symbol exists, cited doc exists, linked test exists, evidence span still matches, contradiction state coherent, scope leak absent, time-bound expiry honored) and the outcome per check. Return a `VerifyExplainResponse` with `status: VerificationStatus`, `checks: Vec<CheckResult>` (each carrying `kind`, `target`, `outcome`, `evidence_ref`), `confidence_delta`, and an `expansion_handle` so the caller can pull richer context.
docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/logs/T59.log:1715:4. Implement `list_memory_conflicts` in `memory_v2/list_memory_conflicts.rs`. Accept `anchor: MemoryId | FileId | SymbolId | DocSectionId`, traverse `contradicts` and `supersedes` link types from Phase 3 memory_links, and return a paginated list of `ConflictRecord`s each carrying `source`, `target`, `link_type` (`contradicts` | `supersedes`), `link_strength`, `created_by`, `created_at`, `link_verification_status`, and `reason`. Honor scope filters per spec §Risks "Scope Leakage."
docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/logs/T59.log:1719:8. In `memory_v2/verify_explain_tests.rs`, write tests that: (a) round-trip each tool's request/response through serde; (b) assert `verify_explain_memory` returns the exact Phase 7 status taxonomy and never invents a new status string; (c) assert every check result carries an evidence reference; (d) assert a memory whose linked symbol was deleted transitions to `stale` with a `linked_symbol_missing` check failure; (e) assert `list_memory_conflicts` returns both `contradicts` and `supersedes` edges with correct directionality; (f) assert scope-leak negative tests; (g) assert the `verify_memory` and `explain_memory` deprecation shims continue to respond and forward correctly.
docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/logs/T59.log:1724:- `daemon/crates/lattice-daemon/src/rpc/memory_v2/list_memory_conflicts.rs` — `list_memory_conflicts` traversing contradiction + supersession links with scope-aware pagination.
docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/logs/T59.log:1725:- `daemon/crates/lattice-daemon/src/rpc/memory_v2/verify_explain_tests.rs` — unit + scope-leak negative tests covering schema, status taxonomy parity with Phase 7, evidence-reference completeness, conflict directionality, and shim forwarding.
docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/logs/T59.log:1731:- `cd daemon && cargo test -p lattice-daemon --lib rpc::memory_v2::verify_explain_tests` — every verify/explain/conflicts test passes (schema, status parity, evidence completeness, conflict directionality, scope-leak negatives, shim forwarding).
docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/logs/T59.log:1738:- No silent error handling — every verifier failure returns a typed error; scope-leak rejections are explicit errors, not empty results.
