+# T75 — Result
+
+## Files created/modified
+
+- `extension/src/review/eventTraceView.ts`
+- `extension/src/review/retrievalExplanationView.ts`
+- `extension/src/review/reviewPanel.ts`
+- `extension/src/review/rpcPayloads.ts`
+- `extension/src/review/i18n/en.json`
+- `daemon/crates/lattice-daemon/src/rpc/memory_v2/get_event_trace.rs`
+- `daemon/crates/lattice-daemon/src/rpc/mcp_schema_tests/round_trip.rs`
+- `daemon/crates/lattice-daemon/src/rpc/memory_v2/consolidate_session.rs`
+
+## Verification commands and outputs
+
+### Task-required verification
+
+1. `test -f extension/src/review/eventTraceView.ts`
+   - Output: `OK:eventTraceView`
+2. `test -f extension/src/review/retrievalExplanationView.ts`
+   - Output: `OK:retrievalExplanationView`
+3. `cd extension && npm run compile`
+   - Output: `tsc -p ./` completed successfully with exit code `0`
+4. `cd extension && npm run lint`
+   - Output: `eslint src --ext ts` completed successfully with exit code `0`
+
+### Additional verification for the event-trace contract fix
+
+1. `cd daemon && cargo test -p lattice-daemon --lib mcp_schema_tests::round_trip::get_event_trace_request_and_page_round_trip`
+   - Output: `1 passed; 0 failed`
+2. `cd daemon && cargo test -p lattice-daemon --lib mcp_schema_tests::render_modes::get_event_trace_renders_compact_full_and_diagnostic_with_handles`
+   - Output: `1 passed; 0 failed`
+3. `cd daemon && cargo build --release`
+   - Output: release build completed successfully
+
+### Deploy
+
+1. `pkill -f lattice && sleep 2`
+   - Output: exited `143` after matching the running `lattice` process
+2. `cp daemon/target/release/lattice extension/bin/`
+   - Output: success
+3. `cp daemon/target/release/lattice ~/.vscode/extensions/lattice.lattice-0.1.0/bin/`
+   - Output: success
+
+## Issues encountered
+
+- The existing daemon `get_event_trace` payload did not include `actor`, `branch`, or `workspace_id`, which the T75 event-trace table is required to render. I added those fields to the MCP response and updated the round-trip test accordingly.
+- The existing daemon tree had an unrelated compile break in `consolidate_session.rs`: `ConsolidationProposalItem` carried `Option<f64>` while the struct and its parent report still derived `Eq`. That blocked the required Rust verification/build steps, so I removed `Eq` from the affected response structs as a build-unblocking integration fix.
+- There is still no public daemon retrieval-explanation MCP tool. The review panel now ships the full `retrievalExplanation` route, typed payload model, sorting/pagination UI, and cross-navigation entrypoint, but when the bridge is asked for a request id it renders a truthful unsupported-state message rather than fabricating ranking data that the daemon does not currently expose.
+
+## Final status
+
+partial
