Implemented the T75 scope in the review panel and wrote the execution report to [T75.md](/home/pete/cadres/lattice/docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/results/T75.md).

The main delivered change is a working Event Trace review surface with filtering, sorting, pagination, payload inspection, and memory-linked navigation, plus the Retrieval Explanation route and UI wiring. I also extended the daemon/event-trace RPC payload so the extension can render actor, branch, and workspace context, and updated the schema round-trip tests accordingly.

Status is `partial`, not `complete`. The retrieval-explanation view is present and integrated, but the daemon still does not expose a real retrieval-explanation RPC/tool, so the UI truthfully renders an unsupported state instead of inventing data. Verification passed for the required file checks, `extension` compile, `extension` lint, the relevant Rust schema tests, and the daemon release build/deploy steps.
